### Unreleased

- Fix `--append` builds handing contested geohash cells to whichever batch ran
  last. Cells that already belong to a better-ranked place (by placetype, then
  population, then centroid distance) now keep their existing owner, so border
  cities no longer resolve to the neighbouring country that happened to be
  processed later (for example Tijuana resolving to San Diego).
- Store `population` and `area` in `compact_places` so append batches can rank
  candidates against previously written places. Existing databases are
  upgraded in place when appending; the new columns are nullable and readers
  are unaffected.

### 1.0.0 - 2018-08-02

- Add bug fix for reverse lookup in rural/remote areas (@cosorio94)
- Upgrade sqlite3 to fix compatability issues with Node v10

### 0.0.1 - 2016-05-05

- Initial release
